# Quick guide template of a thermostat: the "manual" example of stxt-pdf with Slots for what changes from one model
# or edition to another. The instructions, the figures, the wiring and the troubleshooting are part of the template;
# the model, the version of the guide, the contents of the box, the factory schedule, the specifications, the
# warranty and the support contacts come in the data, so one guide serves the models that share the device.
# manual.json has the sample data.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 64 54 66 54
	Title: Quick guide to the ${model} thermostat
	Language: en
	Styles:
		For element: Figure
			Typography:
				Number label: Figure {number}.
		For style: table
			Typography:
				Number label: Table {number}.
	Section:
		Page overlay:
			Id: header
			Offset: -34 0 auto 0
			Stack:
				Horizontal: justify
				Item:
					Text: ${model} · Quick guide · Version ${version}
				Item:
					Text: {heading 2}
		Page overlay:
			Id: footer
			Offset: auto 0 -40 0
			Box:
				Padding: 5 0 0 0
				Border: 0.5 0 0 0
				Border color: #BFD9D7
			Stack:
				Horizontal: justify
				Item:
					Text: Need help? Write to us at ${email}
						Link: mailto:${email}
				Item:
					Text: Page {page} of {pages}
		Block:
			Id: banner
			Style: banner
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 18 0
			Text: Quick guide
				Typography:
					Size: 8
					Bold: true
					Color: #8FD1CC
					Case: uppercase
					Letter spacing: 1.2
			Heading 1:
				Text: ${model} Thermostat
				Box:
					Padding: 0
					Border: 0
					Margin: 0
				Typography:
					Color: #FFFFFF
					Numbered: false
			Text: Install it, connect it to the app and program your home in under half an hour.
				Typography:
					Size: 11
					Color: #C7E4E1
				Box:
					Margin: 4 0 0 0
		Stack:
			Id: overview
			Gap: 26
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 6 0
			Item:
				Figure:
					Id: fig-device
					Alt: The thermostat seen from the front, with its four parts numbered
					Box:
						Width: 250
						Margin: 0
					Caption: The four parts of the thermostat.
					Block:
						Frame:
							Id: device
							Box:
								Width: 250
								Height: 250
							Image: examples/manual/en/thermostat.svg
								Box:
									Width: 100%
							Overlay:
								Offset: 30 auto auto 184
								Style: badge
								Text: 1
							Overlay:
								Offset: 76 auto auto 124
								Style: badge
								Text: 2
							Overlay:
								Offset: 170 auto auto 70
								Style: badge
								Text: 3
							Overlay:
								Offset: 120 auto auto 190
								Style: badge
								Text: 4
			Item:
				Grow: 1
				Block:
					Heading 2:
						Text: Meet your thermostat
						Box:
							Margin: 0 0 8 0
					List:
						Marker: decimal
						List item:
							Paragraph: **Status light.** Solid green when connected to the network; flashes while pairing.
						List item:
							Paragraph: **Current temperature** of the room, in degrees Celsius.
						List item:
							Paragraph: **Target temperature.** The orange dot marks the one you have chosen.
						List item:
							Paragraph: **Dial.** Turn it to raise or lower the temperature and press it to change mode.
		Heading 2:
			Text: In the box
		Grid:
			Id: contents
			Column sizes: repeat(3, *)
			Gap: 10
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 4 0
			Area: [box]
				Block:
					Style: tip
					Text: <item>
						Typography:
							Bold: true
					Text: <detail>
		Block:
			Id: warning-power
			Style: notice
			Text: Warning
				Style: label
			Text: Installation must be carried out by a qualified person. Before touching any wire, switch off the power at the electrical panel and check with a voltage tester that there is no voltage.
		Block:
			Id: installation
			Heading 2:
				Text: Installation
				Box:
					Margin: 0 0 8 0
			Markdown:
				Number markers: decimal
				Content >>
					1. Remove the old thermostat and note which terminal each wire goes to.
					2. Separate the wall plate from the thermostat by gently prying at the bottom.
					3. Screw the plate to the wall, **1.5 m** from the floor and away from drafts and heat sources.
					4. Connect the wires to the terminals following the diagram below and tighten the screws firmly.
					5. Fit the thermostat onto the plate and restore the power: it will switch on by itself.
			Figure:
				Id: wiring
				Caption: Wiring diagram of the four terminals.
				Image: examples/manual/en/wiring.svg
					Alt: Wiring diagram of terminals L, N, C and NO with the wire colors
					Box:
						Width: 100%
			Heading 3:
				Text: If your installation has no neutral
			Markdown:
				Typography:
					Code font: IBM Plex Mono
				Content >>
					The thermostat can run on batteries in homes without a neutral wire. Leave terminal `N` free and see [section {number of: specs-heading}](#specs) to find out which batteries to use. In that case the screen turns off when it is not touched.
			Heading 3:
				Text: Check the connection
			Paragraph: Once installed, the screen should show the time and the temperature. You can check the state of the terminals from the settings menu, with the following sequence:
			Block:
				Id: terminal
				Style: code
				Text:
					Typography:
						Preformatted: true
					Content >>
						> Settings > Service > Terminals

						L     230 V      [ OK ]
						N     0 V        [ OK ]
						C     closed     [ OK ]
						NO    open       [ OK ]
			Block:
				Style: tip
				Text: Tip
					Style: label
					Typography:
						Color: #134E4A
				Text: If a terminal shows in red, check the wire and repeat the check before closing the cover.
			Heading 3:
				Text: Terminal reference
			Figure:
				Id: tab-terminals
				Style: table
				Caption: Thermostat terminals and usual wires.
				Table:
					Id: terminals
					Column sizes: 56 * 100
					Header rows:
						Row:
							Cell: Terminal
							Cell: Function
							Cell: Usual wire
					Body:
						Row:
							Cell: L
								Row header: true
								Style: mono
							Cell: Power supply, live
							Cell: Brown
						Row:
							Cell: N
								Row header: true
								Style: mono
							Cell: Power supply, neutral
							Cell: Blue
						Row:
							Cell: C
								Row header: true
								Style: mono
							Cell: Boiler common contact
							Cell: Gray
						Row:
							Cell: NO
								Row header: true
								Style: mono
							Cell: Normally open contact
							Cell: Yellow
		Block:
			Id: app
			Break:
				Before: page
			Heading 2:
				Text: Connect the app
				Box:
					Margin: 0 0 8 0
			Stack:
				Gap: 24
				Box:
					Margin: 0 0 8 0
				Item:
					Figure:
						Id: fig-app
						Box:
							Width: 112
							Margin: 0
						Caption: The main screen of the app.
						Image: examples/manual/en/app.png
							Id: app-screen
							Alt: The main screen of the app, with the living room temperature and the plus and minus buttons
							Box:
								Width: 112
				Item:
					Grow: 1
					Markdown:
						Number markers: decimal
						Content >>
							1. Download the **Aire+** app from your phone's app store.
							2. Create an account or sign in with the one you already have.
							3. Tap **Add thermostat** and press and hold the thermostat dial for five seconds.
							4. When the light flashes green, choose your Wi-Fi network and enter the password.
							5. Give the room a name, for example “Living room”. Done!

							If pairing fails, bring the phone closer to the thermostat and check that you are using a **2.4 GHz** network: 5 GHz is not supported.
			Heading 2:
				Text: Set your weekly schedule
			Paragraph: The thermostat comes with an energy-saving schedule that you can change from the app or from the dial menu. These are the factory time slots (table {number of: tab-schedule}):
			Figure:
				Id: tab-schedule
				Style: table
				Caption: Time slots of the factory schedule.
				Table:
					Id: schedule
					Column sizes: * * *
					Header rows:
						Row:
							Cell: Time slot
							Cell: Monday to Friday
							Cell: Weekend
					Body:
						Row: [schedule]
							Cell: <slot>
								Row header: true
							Cell: <weekdays>
							Cell: <weekend>
			Heading 2:
				Text: Troubleshooting
			Markdown:
				Table columns: auto
				Content >>
					| Symptom | Probable cause | What to do |
					|---------|----------------|-----------|
					| The screen does not turn on | No power or a loose wire | Check the panel and terminals L and N |
					| Status light in red | No Wi-Fi connection | Move the router closer or pair again |
					| The boiler does not start | C/NO contact wired wrong | Check figure {number of: wiring} (page {page of: wiring}) |
					| Wrong temperature | It is near a heat source | Move it 1.5 m from the floor |
			Heading 2:
				Id: specs-heading
				Text: Technical specifications
			Figure:
				Id: tab-specs
				Style: table
				Caption: Specifications of the ${model}.
				Table:
					Id: specs
					Column sizes: 150 *
					Body:
						Row: [specifications]
							Cell: <name>
								Row header: true
							Cell: <value>
								Style: mono
		Block:
			Id: support
			Heading 2:
				Text: Warranty and support
			Columns:
				Count: 2
				Gap: 26
				Separator: 0.5
				Separator color: #BFD9D7
				Box:
					Margin: 0 0 12 0
				Markdown:
					Content >>
						### Warranty

						The ${model} has a **${warranty}** warranty from the date of purchase, covering any manufacturing defect. It does not cover damage from incorrect installation or damage caused by moisture or impacts. Keep the invoice: we will ask for it to process the warranty.

						### Recycling

						At the end of its useful life, do not throw the thermostat away with household waste. Take it to a recycling center or hand it in at any store when you buy a new one. Batteries are recycled separately.
			Grid:
				Id: contact
				Column sizes: repeat(3, *)
				Gap: 10
				Area:
					Block:
						Style: tip
						Text: Phone
							Style: label
							Typography:
								Color: #134E4A
						Text: <phone>
							Typography:
								Bold: true
								Size: 11
						Text: <phone_hours>
							Typography:
								Size: 8
				Area:
					Block:
						Style: tip
						Text: Email
							Style: label
							Typography:
								Color: #134E4A
						Text: <email>
							Link: mailto:${email}
							Typography:
								Bold: true
								Size: 11
						Text: We reply in less than 24 hours
							Typography:
								Size: 8
				Area:
					Block:
						Style: tip
						Text: Web
							Style: label
							Typography:
								Color: #134E4A
						Text: <web>
							Link: https://${web}
							Typography:
								Bold: true
								Size: 11
						Text: Videos, FAQs and forum
							Typography:
								Size: 8
		Block:
			Id: lists
			Heading 2:
				Text: List of figures and tables
			Text: Figures
				Style: list-label
			Table of contents:
				Id: figures
				Of: figures
			Text: Tables
				Style: list-label
			Table of contents:
				Id: tables
				Of: tables
